sequenceDiagram
    participant A as Request A
    participant DB as seat_inventory row (available = 1)
    participant B as Request B

    rect rgb(255, 235, 235)
    Note over A,B: naive check-then-update (what we do NOT do)
    A->>DB: SELECT available_seats  -> 1
    B->>DB: SELECT available_seats  -> 1
    A->>DB: UPDATE SET available_seats = 0
    B->>DB: UPDATE SET available_seats = 0   (overwrites A: lost update)
    Note over A,B: both requests got the last seat - oversold
    end

    rect rgb(235, 255, 235)
    Note over A,B: atomic conditional UPDATE (inventory-service)
    A->>DB: UPDATE ... SET available_seats = available_seats - 1<br/>WHERE available_seats >= 1
    Note over DB: row lock held by A
    B->>DB: same UPDATE - blocks on A's row lock
    A->>DB: COMMIT (available = 0)
    DB-->>B: WHERE re-checked on the new row: 0 rows updated
    Note over B: 409 SEATS_UNAVAILABLE
    end
